> ontology or `templates/typed_refusals.md.tmpl`, then regenerate.

Every `{:error, _}` this library returns carries an `AshGraphLaw.Refusal` with a
closed `code`, a closed `class`, and the Chatman failure-taxonomy `broken_term` the
refusal witnesses. A refusal is an observation about one exact input. GraphLaw
derives and validates; it never authorizes, so a refusal neither grants nor
withdraws authority.

